---
// The black-box problem. Short, sharp, no fear-mongering.
---

<section class="border-b border-edge-soft bg-void py-20 sm:py-28">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-[1180px] px-5 sm:px-8">
    <div class="grid gap-x-16 gap-y-8 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.1fr] lg:items-center">
      <div class="reveal">
        <h2 class="t-display measure">
          Most cleaners want you to trust a number.
        </h2>
        <p class="t-body-lg measure mt-6">
          The category runs on one move: surface a big
          <span class="font-mono text-ink">“1,000 junk files found”</span>
          figure, a reassuring checkmark, and a Clean button. You never see which
          files, where they live, or why removing them is safe, so the number is
          the only thing you have to go on, and you can't check it.
        </p>
        <p class="t-body measure mt-4">
          That is a bad deal for anyone who knows what lives under
          <span class="font-mono text-ink-2">~/Library</span>. Gargantua takes the
          opposite position: nothing is removable until you can see the evidence.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- the contrast, shown not told -->
      <div class="reveal" style="--reveal-delay: 120ms">
        <div class="grid gap-px overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-edge bg-edge sm:grid-cols-2">
          <div class="bg-surface-1 p-6">
            <p class="t-caption font-mono uppercase tracking-wide text-ink-4">
              Typical cleaner
            </p>
            <p class="mt-4 font-mono text-[2.25rem] font-semibold leading-none text-ink-3 tabular-nums">
              1,000
            </p>
            <p class="t-caption mt-2">junk files found</p>
            <ul class="mt-5 space-y-2.5">
              {
                ["Which files? Hidden.", "Why safe? Marketing copy.", "Reversible? Permanent delete."].map(
                  (line) => (
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2 t-caption">
                      <svg
                        class="mt-px shrink-0"
                        width="13"
                        height="13"
                        viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                        fill="none"
                        stroke="var(--color-ink-4)"
                        stroke-width="2.2"
                        stroke-linecap="round"
                        aria-hidden="true"
                      >
                        <path d="M18 6 6 18M6 6l12 12" />
                      </svg>
                      {line}
                    </li>
                  ),
                )
              }
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-surface-1 p-6">
            <p class="t-caption font-mono uppercase tracking-wide text-accretion">
              Gargantua
            </p>
            <p class="mt-4 font-mono text-[2.25rem] font-semibold leading-none text-ink tabular-nums">
              287
            </p>
            <p class="t-caption mt-2">rules, each one auditable</p>
            <ul class="mt-5 space-y-2.5">
              {
                ["Every item names its rule.", "Rating set before any UI sees it.", "Trash-first, with an audit log."].map(
                  (line) => (
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2 t-caption">
                      <svg
                        class="mt-px shrink-0"
                        width="13"
                        height="13"
                        viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                        fill="none"
                        stroke="var(--color-safe)"
                        stroke-width="2.4"
                        stroke-linecap="round"
                        stroke-linejoin="round"
                        aria-hidden="true"
                      >
                        <path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5" />
                      </svg>
                      {line}
                    </li>
                  ),
                )
              }
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
